Arara Code: extension-owned auxiliary selector action and visibility lock.

Why a patch: stable/proposed extension APIs cannot place a separate action beside
secondary sidebar selectors or prevent native commands, view reveal and maximize
from reopening that workbench part. The extension provides the command, label,
title and codicon through arara.ui.auxiliaryAction{Command,Label,Title,Icon};
arara.ui.auxiliaryBarLocked closes and gates the part until released. All product
state, text and coordination remain in the extension. No process, path or network
operations are introduced. Context keys are window-local and not persisted.
Touches: src/vs/workbench/browser/layout.ts src/vs/workbench/browser/parts/paneCompositePart.ts src/vs/workbench/browser/parts/auxiliarybar/auxiliaryBarPart.ts src/vs/workbench/browser/parts/auxiliarybar/media/auxiliaryBarPart.css

